// TYPOGRAPHY ONLY. This component renders at two call sites with opposite
// layout needs -- a column in the auction side rail, where it is a paragraph
// that may take the height it needs, and a row inside the 70px bid bar, where
// it must be bounded on both axes. A flex shorthand here resolves against
// whichever axis the PARENT happens to run, so the one basis that bounded the
// bar's width made the rail's copy a 240px-tall block for a single sentence.
// The bar's constraints live in auction-main-bid.styl, scoped to the bar.
.auction-settlement-status
  margin-right 10px
  padding 4px 8px
  font-size 12px
  line-height 1.3
  // Was `var(--text-color-secondary)`, a custom property declared in no
  // stylesheet in this repo -- so the declaration was invalid at computed-value
  // time and dropped entirely, and this text had never once rendered in a
  // secondary colour. It greps clean and reads as correct CSS, which is what
  // makes it survive review. This app styles from the stylus tokens in
  // `app/styles/variables.styl`; a CSS custom property here is the exception
  // and has to be declared somewhere before it means anything. The literal
  // below is the same secondary-text value the auction election control uses.
  color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6)
